From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:21:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Fix #1: verify the update installer before running it

The update feed could name any path or URL as the installer and the app
copied and ran it unchecked. Now:

- latest.json parsing lives in Core (UpdateFeed) so it can be tested.
- `installer` must be a bare file name next to latest.json; absolute,
  UNC, relative-with-folders and web addresses are ignored with a logged
  reason.
- Plain http:// feeds and installers are refused; only folders and https.
- `sha256` is required in latest.json and the copied installer is hashed
  and compared before Process.Start; a mismatch deletes the copy and
  tells the person.
- Versions compare on major.minor.build so a 4-part latest.json cannot
  offer the same version forever.
- The confirmation dialog shows where the installer comes from.
- build.ps1 -Installer writes sha256 into latest.json; company/README
  documents the format.

Also covers #20 (file reads/copies off the UI thread) in UpdateService.

Tests: UpdateFeedTests (absolute/UNC/relative/http installers, http
feed, missing or malformed sha256, 4-part version, hash match).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
